    "lawCode": "Amd §96-d, Bank L",
    "lawSection": "Banking Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1936\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the banking law, in relation to multiple branches in\nan existing banking development district\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nIt allows for the establishment of multiple branches in an existing\nbanking development district by a bank, trust company or national\nbank. The purpose of this bill is to encourage banks to expand their\nservices, especially in underdeveloped areas.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nThis bill adds a subdivision that states that nothing shall preclude\nthe establishment of multiple branches in an existing banking\ndevelopment district. Additional approved branches would be eligible\nfor all the rights and privileges authorized by Section 1 of the\nbanking law.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe bill addresses the limitations currently experienced by banking\ninstitutions to expand in banking development districts.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2007-2008 - A.1680\n02/06/08 Passed Assembly\n02/06/08 Delivered to Senate - Referred to Banks\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
